# Editor-first UI (Godot)

- **Do not edit** `.tscn`, `project.godot`, or Input Map definitions in this repo—the user configures those manually. When static UI tweaks are needed (e.g. `mouse_filter`), **tell the user exactly what to set in the Inspector** and let them save the scene.
- **Do not** re-apply those same Inspector settings from `_ready()` / deferred calls **unless** the value truly must come from runtime (loaded data, accessibility toggles, etc.).
- Scripts stay for behaviour: signals, gameplay, orchestration—not for redoing Inspector work the user can freeze in scenes.

Turn-order rows (same pattern anywhere you need one Control to receive hover): root row **Mouse → Stop**; visible child Controls layered on top (**Ignore**) so hover hits the row. User sets those on the nodes in-editor.
